    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92599.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "You asked some serious questions, Ray Chitna Carpenter. First of all, that book was written in a period of intense insomnia. So I wasn't sleeping after we lost our son Tommy on the last day of 2020 and after the nightmare of January 6th. And so I figured I was up all the time and in great pain and anguish about the loss of Tommy. And so I decided that I was going to have to try to record every TTL that I could of his life and what happened. And basically started doing the same thing about January 6, then we'll flip through with the 6th and with the impeachment trial. Speaker Pelosi had asked me to be the lead impeachment manager when we went over to the Senate side to bring the Clinton impeachment against Trump for inciting insurrection against the Constitution",
