    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92599.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "I once saw a speech with Nelson Mandela, but don't quote me on it, maybe I imagined it, but I'm pretty sure I saw it with Nelson Mandela, where he distinguished between optimism and hope. And he said, you know, optimism is almost like a personality trait you're born with. Some people are more optimistic, some people are more pessimistic and That's just in the mysteries and the miracles of heredity and genetics, right? But hope is something anybody can choose. Or with field of truth, you can be an optimist or a pessimist and hope is a decision. It is like telling yourself to go exercise.",
