  {
    "episode_id": 92599,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92599.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "I absolutely love that. I love that distinction. To me, hope is closely related to the acceptance that much of life is uncertain. and that change is inevitable in our lives. It's just like, I'm so afraid of change when I'm in the middle of it. And I think a lot of people feel the same way. And then when you're on the other side of it, it's like, oh, thank God. So hope is related to life being uncertain and change is inevitable. How does your career in life inform how you think about uncertainty?",
