    "turn_idx": 39,
    "turn_text": "And he never gave up on anybody. I always love to tell the story about my dad. We got into an elevator one time. He was one of the founders of Progress and Think Tank called the Institute for Policy Studies. And it was actually, it may have been the first think tank, or at least the first think tank that wasn't dependent on government money. But anyway, we were at his office and we got into this elevator. And there was a guy in there who basically looked like a hell's angel. He was a biker, he had on the bandana, he had tattoos all over his body. And we got in And I'm thinking to myself, my dad's going to talk to him. My dad's going to talk to him. Please don't talk to him. Please don't talk to him. My dad says, hey, he said that you've got all these tattoos all over you. Do you regret having gotten them? It's probably in his 40s and maybe my dad was in his 50s at the time. I think I was 16 years old.",
