    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92599.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 51,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, that's my job. So I thrive on the ability to mobilize the incredible energies and talents of people in my district, the 8th District of Maryland. That's right. Montgomery County, a little piece of Prince George's, but also to draw on the talents and energies from people. around the country and then channel them into progress, which is what politics is all about. I mean, government is not a money-making opportunity for the guy who gets in and his family and his corporations. Government is an instrument for the common good for everybody. It's for uplifting everyone. So I consider it a great blessing to have a job where I can do that. And yeah, maybe that's the reason why in system I'm calling it a hike, because we stopped so much to talk to people. I've got to remind myself I'm trying to exercise.",
