    "turn_text": "I honestly felt like when I was speaking with Jamie, I could have just been right on the trail at Rockby Park, just yammering on with him. He's exactly who he is in person, in real life, in person, you know, away from the screen. And he is a spirit of optimism as he is shared with us and I just feel completely lifted up by our conversation and inspired and emotional. He's been through so much and he has such an open heart and he speaks with that open heart to everyone and to every subject with that open heart as well as an extraordinary intellect and knowledge. I think it's obvious that he's been a teacher for a long time because he finds ways to make complicated things a little easier to understand. And that's a real gift. So I'm so glad that we got the chance to steal him away from his official duties for just a little while. When he shared with us what Nelson Mandela said and the difference between optimism and hope that really rang a bell for me. It makes everything so clear and it helps me understand inside of myself those times in my life when I have been empty without a North Star because I haven't been able to figure out how to get these darker feelings out of my gut and move past them. You know, sometimes you just need a quote from somebody that makes sense to you to help you sort of write yourself. And I feel like Jamie provided that today. Hope is a muscle is produced by Jesse Baker, Eric Newsom, Eleanor Kagan, and he would take a ton. Our sound designer is Kristen Mueller. I'm Mary Chapin Carpenter. Stay mighty. See you the next time.",
